WEBVTT

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:06.410
 الحمد لله و الصلاة و السلام على رسول الله و على آله و صحبه أجمعين

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:10.020
أما بعد السلام عليكم و رحمة الله و بركاته 

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:13.070
I would like to show you the last example of

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:17.000
the case study of progressive arguments inside of a passage.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.017
And this is also taken from Sūrat al-Baqara.

00:00:19.987 --> 00:00:24.890
This is going to start with Āyat al-Kursī (the Verse of the Throne), which is 255, and we're gonna go to 261.

00:00:24.937 --> 00:00:28.447
Verses 251 -261 (from Sūrat al-Baqara). 

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.700
And, uh, I'll try to translate all of it.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.920
Then I'll highlight the progression of one of the several ideas.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.030
There's several things going on in this passage.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.810
If we did all of them, that would take too long.

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:40.930
So I'll only highlight one of the themes

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:43.060
that are being progressed as the āyāt (verses) progress.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.460
اللَّهُ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ هُوَ الْحَيُّ الْقَيُّومُ لاَ تَأْخُذُهُ سِنَةٌ وَلاَ نَوْمٌ 

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:50.700
Allāh: there is no-one to be worshiped or obeyed in any way, shape, or form but He

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:55.990
The Living, the Established, and the Establisher of all-things.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.030
لاَ تَأْخُذُهُ سِنَةٌ وَلاَ نَوْمٌ 

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.060
لَهُ مَا فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَا فِي الأَرْضِ

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:02.290
Slumber nor drowsiness doesn't get a hold of Him; neither does sleep.

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:08.600
He owns exclusively whatever lies in the skies and whatever lies in the earth

00:01:08.579 --> 00:01:11.230
مَنْ ذَا الَّذِي يَشْفَعُ عِنْدَهُ إِلاَّ بِإِذْنِهِ 

00:01:11.209 --> 00:01:16.739
Who dare intercede or make a case before Him except by His permission?

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:19.080
يَعْلَمُ مَا بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ 

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:23.110
He knows what lies ahead of them and what lies behind them. 

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.600
وَلاَ يُحِيطُونَ بِشَيْءٍ مِنْ عِلْمِهِ 

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:27.440
Any they encompass nothing of His Knowledge.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.240
إلا بما شاء : Except for what He Himself has willed.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.620
وَسِعَ كُرْسِيُّهُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالأَرْضَ 

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:36.120
His Throne (Kursī)  extends over the skies and the earth.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:40.190
وَلاَ يَئُودُهُ حِفْظُهُمَا 

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:43.970
And guarding both of them does not exhaust Him.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.130
وَهُوَ الْعَلِيُّ الْعَظِيمُ 

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:46.530
And He is the High, the Great.

00:01:46.547 --> 00:01:47.510
لاَ إِكْرَاهَ فِي الدِّينِ  

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:51.110
There is absolutely no forcing anyone whatsoever in the matter of religion.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.820
قَدْ تَبَيَّنَ الرُّشْدُ مِنْ الغَيِّ 

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:57.660
The correct or straight way has been made abundantly clear and

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.000
distinct from the deviated course.

00:02:00.005 --> 00:02:01.310
فَمَنْ يَكْفُرْ بِالطَّاغُوتِ 

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:06.050
And then whoever were to disbelieve in the forces of rebellion.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:06.830
وَيُؤْمِنْ بِاللَّهِ 

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.910
And instead believe in Allāh.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.440
فَقَدْ اسْتَمْسَكَ بِالْعُرْوَةِ الْوُثْقَى 

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:16.520
Then such a person has held on for dear life to the strongest kind of anchor.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:18.150
لاَ انفِصَامَ لَهَا  

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:23.326
In whose chain there is no chink; there is no break in that chain; it cannot snap.

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.386
وَاللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ 

00:02:25.396 --> 00:02:26.896
 And Allāh is All-Hearing, All-Knowing. 

00:02:26.926 --> 00:02:29.106
اللَّهُ وَلِيُّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا 

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.917
And Allāh is the Protective-Friend of those who believe.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.460
يُخْرِجُهُمْ مِنْ الظُّلُمَاتِ إِلَى النُّورِ 

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:37.800
He pulls them out, or brings them out, of darknesses into Light.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.287
وَالَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا أَوْلِيَاؤُهُمْ الطَّاغُوتُ  

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:44.363
And those who disbelieved: their protective-friends are the rebellious.

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:46.613
يُخْرِجُونَهُمْ مِنْ النُّورِ إِلَى الظُّلُمَاتِ 

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.143
They bring them out of Light into darknesses.

00:02:50.173 --> 00:02:51.993
أُوْلَئِكَ أَصْحَابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيهَا خَالِدُونَ 

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:55.420
Those are the people of fire in which they shall remain.

00:02:55.430 --> 00:03:00.390
أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِي حَاجَّ إِبْرَاهِيمَ فِي رَبِّهِ أَنْ آتَاهُ اللَّهُ الْمُلْكَ إ

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:07.788
Didn't you look at the one that that debated viciously against Ibrahīm (عليه السلام) in the matter of his Master.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:10.900
On account of the fact that Allāh had given him kingdom.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.005
إِذْ قَالَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ 

00:03:12.075 --> 00:03:13.715
When Ibrahīm (عليه السلام) said:

00:03:13.785 --> 00:03:15.605
رَبِّي الَّذِي يُحْيِي وَيُمِيتُ 

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:19.170
My Master is the one who gives life and gives death.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.840
قَالَ أَنَا أُحْيِي وَأُمِيتُ 

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.748
I'm the one who gives life, and I'm the one who gives death.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:29.228
قَالَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ يَأْتِي بِالشَّمْسِ مِنْ الْمَشْرِقِ فَأْتِ بِهَا مِنْ الْمَغْرِبِ ف

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:37.326
Ibrahīm (عليه السلام) said: Allāh is certainly the one who brings the sun out from the east. Go ahead, then, and bring it forth from the west.

00:03:37.306 --> 00:03:38.606
فَبُهِتَ الَّذِي كَفَرَ 

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.220
Thus, the one who disbelieved was stumped.

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:44.460
وَاللَّهُ لاَ يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الظَّالِمِينَ 

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:47.334
And Allāh certainly does not guide the wrongdoing nation.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:49.574
أَوْ كَالَّذِي مَرَّ عَلَى قَرْيَةٍ 

00:03:49.624 --> 00:03:51.464
Or like the one who passed by a town.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.514
قَرْيَةٍ وَهِيَ خَاوِيَةٌ عَلَى عُرُوشِهَا  

00:03:53.604 --> 00:03:55.664
And it was turned over on its rooftops.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:59.134
It was completely dilapidated, destroyed for a long time.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.644
قَالَ أَنَّى يُحْيِي هَذِهِ اللَّهُ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا 

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:05.629
He said, how can Allāh bring this back to lifr after it had died?

00:04:05.679 --> 00:04:08.179
فَأَمَاتَهُ اللَّهُ مِائَةَ عَامٍ ثُمَّ بَعَثَهُ 

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:11.509
Then Allāh gave him death for 100 years and  then raised him back to life.

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:15.339
قَالَ كَمْ لَبِثْتَ قَالَ لَبِثْتُ يَوْمًا أَوْ بَعْضَ يَوْمٍ 

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:18.257
Allāh asked him: how long did you remain?

00:04:18.249 --> 00:04:20.557
He said I remained a day, maybe part of the day.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.787
قَالَ بَلْ لَبِثْتَ مِائَةَ عَامٍ 

00:04:22.783 --> 00:04:26.152
 Allah said: instead you remained for a 100 years.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:29.200
فَانظُرْ إِلَى طَعَامِكَ وَشَرَابِكَ لَمْ يَتَسَنَّهْ 

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:34.082
Take a good look at your at your meal and your drink: they haven't aged.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:35.122
It hasn't aged.

00:04:35.142 --> 00:04:36.322
وَانظُرْ إِلَى حِمَارِكَ 

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:38.056
And now take a look at your mule.

00:04:38.086 --> 00:04:39.976
وَلِنَجْعَلَكَ آيَةً لِلنَّاسِ 

00:04:43.466 --> 00:04:40.006
And I've done so to make you into a miracle for people.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.330
وَانظُرْ إِلَى الْعِظَامِ كَيْفَ نُنشِزُهَا 

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:51.120
And now take a look at the bones: how we are now going to raise them, spring them up.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:52.510
ثُمَّ نَكْسُوهَا لَحْمًا 

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:54.840
Then we're going to dress them with flesh. Kalamata between Allahu.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.010
 فَلَمَّا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُ

00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:59.362
When then, when all of that became abundantly clear to him,

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:02.192
لَهُ قَالَ أَعْلَمُ أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ 

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:06.192
He said: I know for a fact that Allāh is in complete control over all things.

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:08.762
وَإِذْ قَالَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ رَبِّ أَرِنِي كَيْفَ تُحْيِ الْمَوْتَى 

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:12.320
And when Ibrahīm (عليه السلام) said: how do you bring the dead back to life, Master.

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:13.710
قَالَ أَوَلَمْ تُؤْمِنْ 

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:16.440
Allāh said, don't you already believe?

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:17.070
قَالَ بَلَى 

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:17.980
He said: of course!

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:19.910
وَلَكِنْ لِيَطْمَئِنَّ قَلْبِي

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:24.560
No, but just to put my heart at ease, to put my heart at tranquility.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.800
قَالَ فَخُذْ أَرْبَعَةً مِنْ الطَّيْرِ 

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:29.570
So he said: take four birds, four kinds of birds.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:30.913
فَصُرْهُنَّ إِلَيْكَ 

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:34.383
Then incline them towards you, train them to come back to you.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:37.023
ثُمَّ اجْعَلْ عَلَى كُلِّ جَبَلٍ مِنْهُنَّ جُزْءًا

00:05:37.013 --> 00:05:40.980
Then place a portion of each on on the top of multiple mountains.

00:05:40.986 --> 00:05:41.786
ثُمَّ ادْعُهُنَّ 

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.006
Then call on them.

00:05:43.006 --> 00:05:44.206
يَأْتِينَكَ سَعْيًا

00:05:44.186 --> 00:05:45.036
They will come back to you running.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:47.406
[I'm deliberately not explaining, by the way.]

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:50.240
Because I've done a lot of work on Sūrat al-Baqara: shame on you!

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:53.398
وَاعْلَمْ أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ 

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:58.708
And know that Allāh is Mighty; Allāh is the Ultimate-Authority; and that Allāh is Wise.

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:02.050
مَثَلُ الَّذِينَ يُنفِقُونَ أَمْوَالَهُمْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ 

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:05.048
The example of those who spend their money in Allāh's path

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:07.867
كَمَثَلِ حَبَّةٍ أَنْبَتَتْ سَبْعَ سَنَابِلَ 

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:12.437
It's the example of a single seed that sprouts seven years of green.

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:13.447
فِي كُلِّ سُنْبُلَةٍ 

00:06:13.437 --> 00:06:14.809
In every one of those ears

00:06:14.827 --> 00:06:15.847
مِائَةُ حَبَّةٍ 

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.845
Is there a 100 more seeds.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:18.220
Well,

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:20.080
وَاللَّهُ يُضَاعِفُ لِمَنْ يَشَاءُ 

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.100
And, above and beyond that, it is Allāh in fact who multiplies for whoever he wants.

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.249
وَاللَّهُ وَاسِعٌ عَلِيمٌ 

00:06:25.269 --> 00:06:26.919
 And Allāh is Vast, Knowledgeable.

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:28.739
OK, now:

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:31.570
This passage we talked about a lot of things 

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:33.709
And your mind must have gone to tons of stories

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:36.979
Of Ibrāhīm (عليه السلام) and then someone else and then Ibrāhīm (عليه السلام ) again

00:06:37.049 --> 00:06:38.540
 And Āyat al-Kursī!

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:39.620
How's all of it  connected?

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:43.920
I'm just going to highlight one theme that is being developed in the set of these āyāt.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:47.270
There are multiple, but I'm only highlighting one.

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:48.510
We began with Āyat al-Kursī.

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:51.331
اللَّهُ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ هُوَ الْحَيُّ الْقَيُّومُ 

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:57.331
Āllāh: no-one is to be worshiped, obeyed, loved, adorned, in any way shape or form

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:56.350
No one has to be worshiped, obeyed, loved, adored in any way, shape or form.

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:58.881
except He: the Living.

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.051
الْحَيُّ 

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:00.660
Now,

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:03.870
Which means life and death is in whose hands?

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.070
Allāh's hands because he is the source of all life.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:07.850
He is al-Ḥayy.

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:08.860
Now,

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:13.310
When someone believes in Allāh he is holding on to an anchor.

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:15.040
Where's an anchor found?

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:15.810
Yeah,

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:17.080
Ship at sea.

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:18.650
Why would you be holding on to an anchor?

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:19.830
Okay.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:23.050
Are you on the ship or off the ship if you're holding onto an anchor?

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:26.170
You're off the ship and you're drowning and you're about to die.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:30.300
And the only thing keeping you alive is you holding on to an anchor.

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:32.190
Allah is the source of all life.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:33.710
And if you were to believe in Allah,

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.960
you're holding onto the anchor that will keep you alive.

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:38.660
Are you with me so far?

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:42.080
So Allāh is saving your life by giving you faith

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:44.070
Because He is the Living and he's giving you that life.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:48.660
Now, if you were to let go of the anchor, what's gonna happen to you?

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:52.800
You're gonna drown into the depths of the sea.

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:55.945
The deeper you get, at the bottom of the sea

00:07:56.026 --> 00:07:58.185
In the Sūra of Light of all places.

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:00.772
يَدَهُ لَمْ يَكَدْ يَرَاهَا

00:08:00.805 --> 00:08:04.002
When he takes his hand out it is so dark he almost can't even see his own hands.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:07.420
The deeper you drown, the darker it gets. Yes or no? Okay.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:09.150
Allāh is the Protective-Friend

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:12.716
A Friend of those who believe.

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:15.390
He takes them out of darknesses into light.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:17.260
Do you see where this is going?

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:20.803
If you were to drown, you would be in darknesses.

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:24.170
And as you drown deeper does it get darker and darker?

00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:26.490
So it's darknesses.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:30.543
But if you're above the water and you're holding onto the anchor you're still in the light.

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:35.400
And the Ṭāghūt wants to take you out of the light

00:08:35.539 --> 00:08:39.000
Let go, and it wants you to drown in the darknesses.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:41.260
You with me? Okay.

00:08:42.039 --> 00:08:45.160
Do you see how the theme of life is progressing?

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:47.160
Now, look at this.

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:48.920
The next āyah says:

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:53.430
Ibrāhīm (عليه السلام) stands in front of a king and says my Master is one who

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:58.001
يُحْيِي وَ يُمِيت

00:08:58.061 --> 00:09:01.121
My Master is the one who gives life and gives death

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:00.860
and gives death

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:07.018
When you internalise: اللَّهُ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ هُوَ الْحَيُّ الْقَيُّومُ 

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:12.550
You will stand in front of the one who can execute you, and still say Allāh gives life.

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:15.930
You will no longer fear for your life from anyone else.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:18.250
When you will internalise Āyat al-Kursī

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:20.800
You will internalise it the way Ibrāhīm internalised it.

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:23.937
And you will be able to say: رَبِّي الَّذِي يُحْيِي وَيُمِيتُ 

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:25.817
In the face of Nimrūṭ.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:29.189
Even though he will say: أَنَا أُحْيِي وَأُمِيتُ

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:32.199
No, I do. Look: I'm going to execute this prisoner.

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:33.819
And this one I will let go

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.060
And I can do that to you

00:09:35.099 --> 00:09:36.819
أُحْيِي وَأُمِيتُ

00:09:36.839 --> 00:09:42.257
And  you will respond back and say, no: Allāh bring the sun from the East; why don't you bring it from the West?

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:44.640
In other words, you're asking to be killed.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.647
And guess what happens next? He's going to be burned.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:48.020
He's gonna be thrown into a fire.

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:51.280
أَوْ كَالَّذِي مَرَّ عَلَى قَرْيَةٍ

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:54.100
And by the way, when you internalise that Allāh is the source of all life

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:55.500
That's not the only lesson you will learn.

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:58.658
You won't just become brave in the face of the most tyrannical

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:02.325
And speak the truth because Allāh controls and Allāh protects your life; nobody else.

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:06.135
You're holding on to an anchor that will never break.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:07.970
That's not the only lesson you will learn.

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:11.995
You will learn hope from life also because life is nothing without hope.

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:12.540
Why?

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:14.495
Because you should take the other example 

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:18.235
Of someone who passed by a town and it was completely destroyed for centuries.

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:19.770
And he looked at it and said,

00:10:19.815 --> 00:10:23.545
أَنَّى يُحْيِي هَذِهِ اللَّهُ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا 

00:10:23.555 --> 00:10:26.595
How will Allāh bring this to life after it had died?

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:30.835
This has been dead for so long it will never come back to life.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:35.185
The ummah is so corrupted ow can they ever come back to being good again!? We're so far gone.

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:37.470
Do you know the kinds of things Muslims do nowadays?

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:42.320
We're so far beyond it that there is no way this can ever come back.

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:46.464
You are like the one who looked at this destroyed town and said how can this city every live again.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:50.644
It's just broken homes and collapsed roofs. That's all it is.

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:53.184
How can Allah bring this back to life?

00:10:53.194 --> 00:10:57.744
He had to internalise: اللَّهُ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ هُوَ الْحَيُّ الْقَيُّومُ 

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:03.534
And so Allāh gives him death for 100 years, brings him back to life. And he says,

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:06.661
I know Allāh is capable over all things.

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:09.061
That's another lesson you'll learn from al-Ḥayy al-Qayyūm.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:08.830
Um,

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:14.481
You'll have hope that Allāh can revive and restore anything because Allāh gives life: you don't.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:18.481
And then that's not the only lesson you should learn from Allāh being al-Ḥayy.

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:21.700
Because, you know, Allāh being al-Ḥayy should teach you multiple lessons!

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:26.440
Each of the āyāt is going to teach you a separate lesson about Āllāh being al-Ḥayy.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:27.786
And so he says:

00:11:27.806 --> 00:11:31.726
وَإِذْ قَالَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ رَبِّ أَرِنِي كَيْفَ تُحْيِ الْمَوْتَى 

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:33.779
Master, how do you bring the dead back to life? 

00:11:33.829 --> 00:11:35.529
Who asked that question before?

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:40.069
When you understand Allāh being al-Ḥayy, you will know that this is not the only life that there is.

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:45.119
You will internalise that you will be brought back to life again by the Living.

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:48.390
Your life is just as safe after your death

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:53.259
And your revival after your death is just as secure as Allāh is al-Ḥayy.

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:54.459
It's a guarantee.

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:56.279
And so, by the end of it:

00:11:56.319 --> 00:11:57.899
أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ 

00:11:58.040 --> 00:12:00.253
Allāh is the Ultimate-Authority; Allāh is the Wise. 

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:04.114
By the way, the birds that you've trained that come flying:

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:06.820
You go [whistling] and the birds come flying back to you

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:10.134
It's like Allāh teaching us that one day He will call and we will come flying back.

00:12:10.364 --> 00:12:13.670
Because we were actually souls that flew away by the command Allāh

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:16.990
And we fly back to Him, flock back to Him, by His Command.

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:21.140
But I included āyat 261 as part of this progressive passage.

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:24.593
The life, death, life, death, life, death thing is over.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:28.220
He says, the example of those who spend in the path of Allāh is like a seed

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:29.170
which, by the way, is dead.

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:33.403
But when it's put in the ground, Allāh gives it what?

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:36.093
Life. And it turns into 700 seeds.

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:38.740
Allah will take your deeds, your charities,

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:42.649
and He will pour a life into them that you cannot, only Allāh can.

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:46.419
Allāh can take take your actions that you may not see the effect of

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:48.940
because they were just a seed, and a seed is buried

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:50.550
which means you don't know what's happening underground.

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:53.980
And the seed may come out of the ground way after you're dead.

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:55.800
But it has life in it.

00:12:55.950 --> 00:13:00.170
You no longer have life in you. You're in the grave. But the seed you planted,

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:02.550
the good you did, has a life of its own.

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:04.780
And it will produce 100 seeds.

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:08.150
Each one of those 100 seeds will have a life that Allāh will give them of their own,

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:12.050
And Allāh is Vast, Knowledgeable in the way he gives life to these seeds.

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:13.450
Life--

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:15.730
what started with Āyat al-Kursī

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:20.360
continuously progressing through a number of āyāt until we get to infāq (spending), subḥānallāh.

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:24.940
Okay, so this idea of progressing notions, 

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:28.170
progressive ideas inside passages is is a very powerful one.

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:31.270
It is one of the dimensions of the logic of the Qur'ān.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:35.900
How the Qur'ān wants to us to build conceptual frameworks of different things.

00:13:35.900 --> 00:13:39.950
Spiritual realities, you know, faith realities, historical realities.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:43.670
You know, how how he wants us to build ideas atop one another.

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:47.452
This, you know, one of the things that I'm a big advocate of,

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:52.332
And that Allāh Himself says, Allāh doesn't advocate knowing the Qurān.

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:54.982
Allāh advocates thinking.

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:56.820
There's no much, 

00:13:56.862 --> 00:13:58.212
أَفَلَا تَعْلَمُوْن

00:13:58.240 --> 00:13:59.180
What do you find?

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:00.832
أَفَلاَ تَعْقِلُونَ 

00:14:00.912 --> 00:14:03.412
Why don't you think? Why don't you think? Why don't you think? 

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:05.993
Ponder, reflect, think.

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:06.663
Contemplate. 

00:14:06.693 --> 00:14:09.193
These are the words that keep occurring in the Qur'ān.

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:11.620
Knowing? Yeah, okay, the basics.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:14.480
The one who knows a lot; the one that doesn't know a lot. Knowledge is there.

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:16.870
But actually, it is what you do with that knowledge.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.170
And the only thing you're supposed to do with that,

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:22.300
The first you're supposed to do with that knowledge is think about it.

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:26.894
There are so many who can acquire the knowledge, repeat the knowledge, like a parrot,

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:28.714
teach it to others, also,

00:14:28.754 --> 00:14:30.894
but never actually sit and what?

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:33.160
Think about what it's saying.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:36.827
To accept, like Imām Ḥamīd al-Dīn al-Farāḥī was saying

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:41.495
You've accepted that others thought about it, that's good enough for me.

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:40.750
Mhm.

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:44.835
You were commended to think. You were commended to ponder. 

00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:47.630
And when that happens, then the Qur'ān, the Word of Allāh.

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:49.780
The Revelation comes to life for you.

00:14:49.790 --> 00:14:51.340
That's when it brings life into the hearts.

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:57.580
So this was our first half of the study of coherence within passages.

00:14:57.590 --> 00:14:58.670
Progressive arguments.

00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:01.240
This was the last of the progressive arguments that I wanted to share with you.

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:03.160
And now we're going to move on to

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:07.060
symmetry and ring composition and structures that are inside of passages.

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:10.230
It's a little bit more elaborate for me to teach, so I'm going to use the visuals,

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:11.750
the laptop to try to teach them.

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:13.460
and type them up as I go.

00:15:13.460 --> 00:15:15.770
So I can I can help you understand it better, Inshāllāh,

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:20.272
So we'll take a couple of minutes and set that up and then we'll reconvene.